summary:
  The codec helper looks for frames inside an ID3 tag.

history:
  A tag can carry anything, a picture for one, and bytes in it can read
  as frames of the other codec. The stream begins where the tag says it
  ends.

target:
  package/contents/ui/streamkind.py

find:
          start = 10 + ((data[6] << 21) | (data[7] << 14) | (data[8] << 7) | data[9])

replace:
          start = 10

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_streamkind.py::test_what_a_tag_holds_is_not_the_stream.
